maya: WIP starter: Next.js + LangChain + small eval harness. Running on Vercel Edge and hitting a repetitive auth/retry loop when the serverless API calls the Redwood SDK. Logs show 401 then immediate retry. Repo: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-lc-eval-starter
ashwin: paste the API route and the exact error please — edge vs node server matters for envs
maya: log snippet:
```
Request to /api/generate failed: 401 Unauthorized
redwood-sdk-js retrying request (attempt 3)
```
API route (simplified):
```js
// pages/api/generate.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_REDWOOD_API_KEY })
export default async function handler(req,res){
  const resp = await client.chat.create({ model: 'l2-small', input: req.body.prompt })
  res.json(resp)
}
```
sophie: two immediate red flags: 1) NEXT_PUBLIC_ keys get bundled to the client, 2) on Edge runtimes secret bindings behave differently. If the key is wrong, the SDK's retry wrapper will keep retrying until max attempts, causing noisy logs.
ashwin: short fix: use a server-only env var and configure the SDK to not retry on 401. Example:
```js
// server/utils/redwoodServerClient.js
import { RedwoodClient } from '@redwood/sdk'
export function getServerClient(){
  return new RedwoodClient({
    apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY,
    retry: { statusCodes: [429, 502, 503], maxRetries: 2 }
  })
}
```
Then import getServerClient in the API route. Also double-check the file has runtime: 'nodejs' if you need Node semantics.
maya: that was it  I accidentally followed an example that used NEXT_PUBLIC_ for convenience. Switched to REDWOOD_API_KEY and adjusted retry policy, redeployed to Edge, and the 401/retry loop disappeared. Thanks! :rocket:
sophie: nice. Can we add a lightweight CI smoke test for the sample repo that hits /api/generate with a mocked client (so we catch auth regressions)? Also add a lint rule or unit test to detect server clients constructed from NEXT_PUBLIC_ env vars.
maya: opening PR with fix + test + README note: https://github.com/redwood-inference/next-lc-eval-starter/pull/12
devex-bot: Created issue #217 in next-lc-eval-starter: "Avoid NEXT_PUBLIC_ for server SDK keys; add CI smoke test for /api/generate"
maya: will also add a tiny eval harness that runs in CI to validate tokenized outputs for the generate route so demos don't silently regress.
